well first of all the government takes  this very seriously and i can understand  that your your viewers and you will be  concerned about this new variant that's  why we've introduced a range of new  restrictions already which we think are  proportionate for example in relation to  travel and in relation to mask wearing  that's why we analyze the the virus and  that's happening for example at portland  down now  but in the meantime the message to  people i think is  fairly straightforward which is keep  calm carry on with your christmas plans  we've put the necessary restrictions in  place but beyond that keep calm and  carry on it's interesting you say carry  on with your christmas plans this is  exactly what the prime minister boris  johnson's also saying saying go ahead  with your christmas parties if you so  wish but actually jenny harris who's of  course the head of the uk health  security agency says that people should  cut back on unnecessary socializing over  the festive period but on the other hand  the prime minister's saying go ahead and  party on so  it seems that you're out of step then  with what the scientists are saying  well well all of our  advice is based on scientific evidence  and indeed the the chief medical officer  and the chief scientific advisor attends  cabinet was at cabinet when we discussed  this earlier this week that's why we've  gone for this balanced and proportionate  set of measures so it is the case that  unlike previously in england people will  have to wear masks on public transport  and they'll have to wear masks in retail  settings we've very much timed up the  border restrictions but beyond that  we believe that those are necessarily  appropriate steps but beyond that people  can carry on with their plans as before  so i would say to people just keep calm  carry on with your christmas plans as as  already set out this morning we're just  learning this actually quite a large  number of organizations a few are  canceling their plans and people are not  listening to what you're saying do you  think that people are just not trusting  what you're saying they just don't have  much confidence so in what you're saying  so some of the people we're hearing  university college london nhs trusts age  uk these are all organizations  government departments that have  cancelled their christmas parties  despite the fact that you're saying  carry on  well i understand that people have um  concerns around the new variant that's  why the government has taken the sort of  measures that we've  already outlined but but beyond that as  the prime minister has been at pains to  say several times and said again  yesterday and i'm very happy to  to repeat again this morning we think  those are sufficient at this stage and  beyond that people should continue with  their plans as intended  we've always said that we want people to  have a better christmas than they had  last year we're confident they're able  to do so but the reason people are able  to do so is because of this vaccine so  the one thing that everyone can do if  they're worried is to make sure that  they take that booster that they make  sure that they top up their immunity and  for example the results out this morning  are very promising about the effects of  that booster they vindicate the decision  taken by the government to invest in  buying those doses of pfizer and moderna  so provided people take the booster when  they get the call provided they abide by  the existing rules as as updated in  light of the the new variant i think  people can continue with their christmas  plans and i'd encourage people to do so  well talking about the fact that um a  number of government organizations have  decided to cancel their christmas party  this is certainly having a knock-on  effect financially on the hospitality  industry which is already taking a huge  bathroom during this pandemic are you  going to provide any support for them  during this winter months well we've  already provided a huge amount  well i think the the the support that  we've outlined and by the way some of  that support is is ongoing still for  example in relation to to business rates  been businesses are still benefiting  from that  beyond that we have not changed the  advice around people  uh taking part in hospitality so going  to the pub going to restaurants and so  on and actually i think most pubs and  restaurants up until very recently have  been doing very well during this season  and we're not discouraging people from  continuing to do so they are going to  take a hit though if a lot of people are  canceling their christmas um you know  plans they will be taking a huge hit a  lot of people had been  relying on this christmas festive  season to make up some of the losses  that they've made they've made over the  years so  will you provide extra support for them  during this christmas period well let's  wait and see how we we do over the the  christmas period because the  government's position remains that  people should carry on with their  christmas plans and i understand why  your viewers and and why people up and  down the country will be concerned about  this new variant i want to reassure  people that that is why we have taken  the measures in relation to to travel  that's why we've tightened some of the  rules around mask wearing but why we're  taking a proportionate approach whilst  we consider  the effects of this this variant and  what  and by that i mean that the uh port and  down and others are examining this for  us to understand exactly it's its  implications whilst that's going on we  believe these are neces these are  appropriate steps they're sufficient for  now to enable people to continue with  their christmas plans as before okay now  we're just hearing of families who are  being stranded in south africa obviously  it's on the redless country and this is  because they're not  enough hotel rooms for them to  quarantine in when they reach the uk so  it looks like a lot of people will be  spending their christmases in those  southern african countries which you  have put on the red list and it appears  that you put the restrictions in place  overnight but you didn't readjust or  look out for the um capacity for the  existing infrastructure plan  well we do have to take the risks  associated with this new variant  seriously and i don't want to impose any  restrictions the government doesn't want  to impose any more restrictions than  necessary but because of the uh origins  of this virus in southern africa we had  to move rapidly to um impose those  restrictions on south africa that's why  we did it immediately of course we'll  make sure that the appropriate  facilities are in in place for people  but the reason why we did that and the  reason this whole strategy is about  making sure that we limit uh the spread  of the omnichrome omicron variant at  this stage whilst we we look at the  effects of it which in turn enables me  to be able to say that people can keep  calm and carry on with their christmas  plans because we're taking tough  measures in relation to the virus coming  into the country through at-risk  countries so you have enough rooms  available then if people in southern  africa are wanting to come here and to  isolate in hotels will there be enough  hotel rooms well of course there's a  difference in the between um  nationals of southern african countries  who are not allowed to come here uk  nationals  who are returning yes of course we'll  make sure that we we have appropriate  provisions so those people who are  stranded we can say to them come home  it's absolutely fine the minister says  there will be enough rooms for you yes  so  so what i say to those people is clearly  they have to abide by the new rules  which means that when they return they  have to immediately hotel quarantine  they have to have their pcr on day two  and day eight and of course we will make  