islation because it's essential to  tackle this problem the turnout was very  low wasn't it it was only 34  yes i mean it is the case that in  by-elections turnout tends to be low but  against that backdrop we we managed to  secure 50 and i really want to thank the  people of bexley for putting their faith  in louis and putting their faith in the  government let's talk about the french  prime minister then rejecting boris  johnson's call for joint uk french  patrols in the channel  we have a crisis here don't we and the  two people who should be coming together  to solve this are just not getting along  where do we go from here  well there's two elements first of all  we need to get our laws in the right  place so they're not currently fit for  purpose and that's why we're bringing  forward the the nationality and balls is  built for example which will uh increase  to a maximum life sentence for those  vile people traffickers who are  exploiting vulnerable people crossing  from one safe country france to another  safe country the uk it has a range of  other measures for example in relation  to increasing the sanctions for  illegally entering the uk so it's  essential we get that through and it's  essential by the way we get support from  other parties for that when that comes  before parliament next week we also have  to have international cooperation now  the home secretary is already this week  has been meeting i believe with her  dutch counterparts and with her italian  counterparts to stop this flow of  migration and we continue to cooperate  with the french we cooperate with the  french in many different ways including  in uh in nato uh in relation to uh joint  intelligence operations so there's a lot  of anglo-french cooperation going on and  actually if you look we have managed  through that corporation to stop 20 000  boats crossing the channel i hope that  cooperation will continue  do you think that the allegations of  fleas and also the crisis that we're  seeing over the migrants issue in the  channel will haunt you when it comes to  the next election general election well  i think it's essential that we address  the  uh challenge of of migrants the the um  the small boats but that is precisely  why we're bringing forward this  legislation to toughen up our laws next  week so the challenge is will other  parties support us in that legislation  will the liberal democrats enable  supporters in that legislation when it  comes before parliament next week

